  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PADEO event</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Programmatic Approach for Sustainable Economic Development (PADEO) forms an important pillar in the Netherlands bilateral relationship with the the Netherlands embassy (EKN) in order to create sustainable solutions to local needs that contribute to local private sector development and strengthen the projcet partners&apos; interventions on SDG 8.The PADEO event is part of the implementing strategy of this focus, through challenges, new ideas and solutions that are identified and developed based on the needs and priorities of local communities, and the networking opportunities that are created. The project partners aim to build and strengthen the collaboration between EKN, the Dutch Ministry of Foreign Affairs&apos; Sustainable Economic Development Department (DDE) and the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO) and create a PADEO community including external partners and stakeholders.The purpose of the PADEO event is to come to a shared vision for those directly involved with PADEO within the eleven countries taking into account the specific characteristics of each country, so that it can be disseminated to our broader network of RVO actors/initiatives and other third parties. The PADEO event gives the PADEO teams the opportunity to inspire, enthuse, exchange knowledge and lessons learned with each other, but also connect with other relevant stakeholders in order to find synergy and to further develop the PADEO approach for the future.</narrative>
  </description>
